# Committed data artifacts are text, normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# The section scripts write their CSVs through Python's `csv` module, whose lineterminator is CRLF
# on every platform, while some artifacts were committed LF -- so the tree held 11 CRLF files and 6
# LF ones by nothing more than which writer touched each one last, and a regeneration rewrote every
# line of a file whose numbers had not moved. That is the diff an audit most needs to be able to
# trust, so the convention is enforced here, once, for every writer rather than in each script.
*.csv text eol=lf

# Keep the rest of the text tree normalised on the same terms.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.lean  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.cff   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# Figures and archives are binary -- never touch them.
*.png   binary
*.tar   binary
*.gz    binary
